*.csv
# Blanket rule above targets generated eval/benchmark noise (root-level
# evaluation_results*.csv / checkpoints_for_eval*.csv, scripts/benchmark_*.csv,
# etc.) — any bare *.csv elsewhere is disposable output, not a committed
# artifact. The few CSVs that ARE committed source-of-truth are force-tracked
# below so the "what's intentionally tracked" policy is visible here instead
# of only in git history:
# - the thesis eval manifest is the committed record of which checkpoints
#   constitute the thesis comparison (see evaluate_all.py --manifest).
!experiments/thesis_eval_manifest.csv
# - append-only sweep run ledger across both training PCs (see
#   sweeps/RESULTS_SCHEMA.md / sweeps/EXPERIMENT_LOG_monolithic.md).
!sweeps/all_runs.csv
# - frozen CLARIN dev/test fragment split assignment (see
#   asr_pipeline/SCOPE.md).
!asr_pipeline/eval/clarin_split.csv
# - generated thesis artifacts (param-count manifest etc.) written by
#   scripts under docs/generated/ (see scripts/model_manifest.py).
!docs/generated/*.csv
# - frozen W&B curve extracts backing the ch5 figure scripts
#   (scripts/thesis_figures/) — the figures must be regenerable without W&B.
!scripts/thesis_figures/data/*.csv

/.cache

/.claude

# Thesis vault (symlink to Windows filesystem, tracked by its own git repo)
/thesis

*.nsys-rep


/evaluate

/docs/deep_research
/docs/sweep_plan

# webapp build artifact (regenerable via webapp/examples_build.py; machine-absolute paths)
webapp/examples_manifest.json

# On-device browser demo: an experiment that nothing else depends on. Moved off
# main on 2026-09-04; the full tree lives on branch `experiment/webapp-ondevice`.
# Ignored here so that a leftover working copy (~300 MB of ONNX blobs kept so the
# branch is runnable on checkout) stays invisible on main.
webapp_ondevice/
